## 2. This fork

**Look4Sat 4.4.9, modified; maintained by BA7OPF <ba7opf@users.noreply.github.com>.**

    Modified version of record: https://github.com/dbdujiaze321/loos4sat-894367

The base of this tree is upstream tag 4.4.9 (commit history starts at
`chore: import Look4Sat 4.4.9 upstream and port stage 1-3 groundwork`).
Everything below was added or changed on top of that tag.

### 2.1 Pass analysis

* New full-screen pass analysis, opened from the chart icon on a pass row.
  Geometry (AOS, TCA, LOS, max elevation, azimuth at TCA, min range, peak range
  rate, azimuth sweep, sunlit fraction), orbital elements, an elevation profile,
  a Doppler plan, a polar sky track and a sampling table, all drawn on a Compose
  `Canvas` with no charting dependency.
* Closest approach is refined by ternary search to ±100 ms instead of taking the
  best sample, and the search is bracketed around the sampled minimum so a
  two-day deep-space window cannot send it wandering.
* Transponder Doppler uses a scaled inverting mapping
  `tx = upHigh - (rx - downLow) * (upWidth / downWidth)`, which reduces to the
  usual sum rule only when both bands are equally wide.
* CSV export: RFC 4180 quoting, UTC ISO 8601 timestamps, metadata in comment
  lines so the file has exactly one header row.
* Calendar export (`.ics`): RFC 5545, CRLF line endings, `VALARM` lead time
  reusing the pass-alarm setting.
* "Track only this satellite" action that reduces the selection to one object.

### 2.2 Data handling

* Saved observing sites (`StationBook`): named coordinates with a derived
  Maidenhead locator, stored as JSON, switchable in one tap. Switching moves the
  station position and the active id in a single write.
* TLE import from pasted text, through the same parser and merge
  rules as file import, so a stale paste cannot overwrite fresher elements.
* TLE parser rewritten to scan for `1`/`2` pairs instead of chunking raw lines
  by three: one blank line in a pasted TLE used to shift every following block
  and silently discard the rest of the file.
* CSV reader now honours RFC 4180 quoting; `"CSS, (TIANHE)"` used to shift every
  following column by one.
* Catalogue export as CSV, written with the importer's own column names so the
  file round-trips instead of being a one-way report.
* A self-trained staleness model (below) and an accuracy budget that triggers a
  data refresh when predicted pass-time error exceeds ten seconds.

### 2.3 Accuracy work

* A power-law model of prediction error against element age,
  `sigma(age) = 0.0208 * age^2.726` seconds, fitted to thirteen measurements of
  two real ISS element sets 8.32 days apart. Residual: 6% mean, 13% worst case.
* The coefficients are retrained on device: every time an element set is
  replaced by a newer one, the old set's along-track error at the new epoch
  becomes one labelled sample, and a closed-form log-log regression refits the
  model. Only tracked satellites are measured.
* Workbench and analysis screen show the predicted error next to the data age;
  the value turns red past the ten-second budget.
* Deep-space correctness fixes: statistics no longer count a geostationary
  ±24 hour placeholder window as 48 hours of visible time; deep-space AOS/LOS
  labels carry the date instead of repeating the same clock time.

### 2.4 UI and accessibility

* Workbench landing page: next pass countdown, best passes in the next 24 hours,
  data freshness, window statistics.
* Per-token theme overrides with JSON import/export, grouped satellite list with
  category icons.
* `IconCard` gained a `contentDescription` parameter; before this, every icon
  button in the app was announced as "button" by screen readers.
* Launcher icon and launch screen are rounded squares. Adaptive icons were
  removed and the SplashScreen compat library was dropped, because it masks the
  icon to a circle on every API level below 31.
* Chinese localisation for all strings added by this fork.

### 2.5 Build and tests

* Version catalog, convention plugins, R8 rules, and a release signing config
  read from `keystore.properties` that is absent on a clean checkout (the build
  then produces an unsigned APK rather than failing).
* 202 unit tests in `core:domain` and 41 in `core:data`. The orbital kernel, the
  merge engine, the alarm policy, the drift/statistics maths and the CSV/ICS
  writers are pure JVM code and are covered without a device.
* `PropagatorConsistencyTest` pins down two properties that were previously
  only assumed: results do not depend on query order (cold, warm, forwards,
  backwards within 1e-6 degrees), and the AOS found by the pass scan sits on the
  horizon for the sampler as well.

### 2.6 What this fork did not do

* No proprietary or closed-source component was added. There is no analytics,
  no telemetry, no advertising and no network call other than the element-set
  downloads the user triggers or that the configured auto-update performs.
* The absolute accuracy of SGP4 against a precise ephemeris is still unverified:
  no public precise-ephemeris source was reachable from the build environment,
  so no "one arcsecond" claim is made anywhere in this tree.

